From 724ee79a6c336017392bdef9af19b53240abff43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:13:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Kanban ratio routing: review follow-ups (fault guards, one
 pool load, per-pool freshness)

- record_run_route keeps its never-raises promise: the ratio receipt block and
  the in-tick start count run under their own logged guards. A failing
  begin_tick (its PRAGMA) is logged with its traceback in run_owned_tick and
  the tick goes on, with ratio routing failing open until a tick starts
  cleanly (off_this_tick).
- A pick loads each candidate credential pool once: live_pool_serving already
  includes the quota_unavailable check live_quota_wall repeated.
- fresh_v2 also requires each pool's own reading (its read_at, else the legacy
  provider block's) within 20 minutes; assemble_v2 carries unread pools forward
  under a fresh computed_at.
- The binary-search docstring says out-of-order rows it skips are not counted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
